cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AccessGroundBench, please cite it as below."
title: "AccessGroundBench: measuring VLM UI grounding under Android accessibility settings"
abstract: >-
  AccessGroundBench measures whether Android accessibility layout settings
  (increased font scale, increased display density, and colour-vision filters)
  degrade a vision-language model's ability to ground UI text — that is, to
  return the pixel coordinates one would tap to hit a named on-screen element.
  It uses a paired within-subject design: the same model answers the same target
  query on a baseline screenshot and on each accessibility-modified screenshot of
  the same screen, and the difference is tested with a pooled cluster permutation
  test over targets, with per-model McNemar tests as a secondary analysis.
type: software
authors:
